#!/usr/bin/python3
"""KantanOS Windows virtual machine.

For Windows programs that Wine cannot run. Windows 11 runs in a QEMU virtual machine owned
by the user (no admin rights, no libvirt): Secure Boot firmware, a software TPM 2.0 chip, a
private network whose only way in is Remote Desktop on 127.0.0.1. Windows programs open
through FreeRDP's RemoteApp mode as ordinary windows on the KantanOS desktop, with the home
folder shared as \\\\tsclient\\home. The VM pauses after ten idle minutes and shuts Windows
down cleanly when the user logs out.

The user brings their own Windows 11 ISO from Microsoft and their own licence; KantanOS never
downloads or ships Windows. Not for anti-cheat games (those need a real Windows install).

  windows-vm setup           guided setup, or a menu of actions once Windows is installed
  windows-vm desktop         the whole Windows desktop in a window
  windows-vm app <id>        one Windows program (ids come from the app list)
  windows-vm scan            refresh the Windows programs in the KantanOS app menu
  windows-vm start | stop | status | password | remove
"""
